  "identifier": "ehrbase",
  "name": "EHRbase",
  "description": "Open-source openEHR Clinical Data Repository (CDR) providing a standard-based backend for interoperable clinical applications. Implements the openEHR Reference Model (RM 1.1.0) and Archetype Definition Language (ADL 1.4), exposing the standardised openEHR REST API and AQL (Archetype Query Language) for structured clinical data storage and retrieval. Backed by PostgreSQL, deployable via Docker or binary. Jointly developed by Vitasystems GmbH and the Peter L. Reichertz Institute for Medical Informatics (TU Braunschweig / Hannover Medical School). Used by hospitals, regional eHealth programmes, and vendors building on the openEHR ecosystem. Apache 2.0, 367 stars, v2.31.0.",
